# Project context (buildwithduy)

Cursed UI experiments site. Categories so far: `birthday`, `payment`, `authentication` (renamed from `password`). Idea backlog lives in the **personal** Cursor AgentStore file `cursed-ideas.md` — keep it private; do not commit or publish.

## Site

- `/` = homepage from `readme.md` (not a category). Logo → `/`.
- Category pages: fixed left sidebar + scrolling content panel (`category-directory.tsx`).
- New builds: route `src/app/{category}/{build}/page.tsx` + registry in `src/lib/builds.ts` + hover demo in `BuildShortcut` + sitemap check.
- Wire build pages through `BuildExperience` (supports `?creator=true`).
- Static assets for a category go under `public/{category}/`.

## Authentication builds

Fake “sign in” shells that resolve via a cursed challenge, then show success.

- Phone demo number: `0123456789` (readonly). Prefer phone over username/password unless the gag needs credentials.
- Primary CTA: dark zinc pill (`bg-zinc-900` / `text-white`), label like `verify with otp`.
- Success copy: `you're checked in` (lowercase). Typical phases: `login` → challenge → `checked-in`.
- Card shell: `rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 bg-white … shadow-sm`.
- Form inputs: `rounded-xl` (not pills). Action buttons stay `rounded-full`.
- Modals (OTP hint, plan picker, etc.): `createPortal` to `document.body`; ~220ms fade via `modalMounted` + `modalActive`; Escape closes; double-rAF to activate after mount.
- OTP/games: collect digits through the interaction (catch, dial, eat, fish, …). Prefer any-order / any-valid-digit unless the gag needs a specific code. Numbers use `font-sans` tabular nums — never mono/display.
- Ship the `{name}-demo.tsx` hover thumbnail with the build (`group-hover` motion; no idle loops).

## Birthday / creator

- Public builds: full date interaction. Creator filming: `?creator=true` → name + birth-year form; year field opens year-only modal via `BuildExperience` / `YearPickerProps`.
- Date thumbnails: today’s date from `src/lib/today.ts` + `suppressHydrationWarning`.

## Tone

- Everything lowercase in UI copy.
- Keep gags readable and short; polish interaction feel over extra chrome.
- Prefer CSS/`group-hover` motion; real game loops only when the build is an actual mini-game (snake, fishing, falling numbers).
